<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8299" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεξ-έλεγκτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>incapable of disproof</i>
			or <i>criticism,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν λόγον ἀ. ποιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>SE</u>
					176b24
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μᾶλλον ἢ πιθανήν</span>
			<i>difficult to disprove</i> rather than credible, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.40
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἔχει τὸ
			ἀνδρεῖον</span> leaves their courage <i>without any real
			test</i> or <i>proof,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.126
			</span></i>; <i>unrefu'ed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.547
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					10.8
				</span></i>
			, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				7.191.2
			</span></i>. of persons, <i>not to be convicted,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				2.1.10
			</span></i>: of conduct, etc . . <i>blameless, unexceptionable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				13.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				25.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pel.</u>
				4
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
